From 6cdada7da004805fcf9090e452d8d2722c61a47e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:11:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wmt: bind one captured ioctl pair to its worker and common
 OFF

Record one exact native Wi-Fi ON/OFF ioctl pair and bind each request
through operation allocation, queue offer, actual worker entry and
completion, waiter result and ioctl return. Link the OFF worker to
one synchronous common/provider scope. A reset, conflicting function
request, bad completion or failed record permanently invalidates capture.

Keep task references across identity comparisons, clear the operation
pointer before caller release and rely on the preceding operation
ownership repair. Failed scopes retain at most two request task pins
until recovery. No pointers or task identifiers enter retained bytes.
The observer changes no native return, queue, reset or hardware operation.

These unselected hooks are an experiment archive, not upstream submission.
Controller/firmware attribution, concurrent resource exclusion, full
kernel linking and device admission remain separate. This synthetic
author is non-certifying and supplies no DCO sign-off.
